# Milestone 33. The build context is an allowlist of source; everything else stays on the host.
# Secrets, local transcripts and personal agent settings must never reach a build stage, because a
# later COPY, a cached layer or a Next/Vite build reading `.env*` could embed them in an image.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.npmrc
!tsconfig.base.json
!apps/
!packages/
!docker/

# Credentials and local configuration, including the committed examples (images take config at run time).
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Agent transcripts, session artifacts and personal or generated agent instructions.
**/.claude
**/.claude-agent-sdk
**/.codex
**/.agents
**/.local
**/sdk-transcripts
**/*.transcript.jsonl
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# Host build output, dependencies and test artefacts: images rebuild from the lockfile on Linux.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/next-env.d.ts
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/generated
**/.npm-cache
**/.cache

# Tests, end-to-end suites and evaluation data are run by CI, not shipped.
apps/web/e2e
apps/*/test
apps/api/lib/testing
packages/*/test
apps/web/playwright.config.ts
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
